// d4r engine, preset M: the input stage, written from the algorithm in M_NOTES.md. Per render pixel it gathers
// 20 features (the colour, four colours of the previous result along three motion candidates, the recurrent
// feature, a motion-change measure), rounds them to FP8 with NGX's dither, and embeds each 2x2-pixel token
// (128 feature slots) into 64 channels with one matrix product per 4x4-token block. It also writes the three
// motion candidates the reconstruction uses.
// DOT2: the same stage for GPUs without cooperative matrices or FP8 (RDNA2): the product on v_dot2_f32_f16 with the
// same binary16 rounding after every 32 products, FP8 in binary16 and integer arithmetic (fp8_soft.glsl); binding 10
// holds the matrix widened to binary16 pairs [64][64] by the runtime. A workgroup is four of the blocks (2x2), so the
// product runs with a token per lane and wave-uniform weights (one block: per-lane weights, 3.4x the product's time).
// It skips the slot pairs that are always zero (6 of a pixel's 16, enc0_features.glsl: their products add +0, the
// output is the same) and reuses the previous result's sample of candidates along the same vector (ENC0_DEDUP):
